{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"# HANDOFF — this epic's work stops here and passes to a NEW session\n\nOperator stop order. Nothing was pushed or submitted. This comment is the scoreboard and the\nrecovery recipes the incoming session needs.\n\n## Scoreboard\n\n| ticket | state | note |\n|---|---|---|\n| **this epic** (`0e68`) | `in_progress`, assignee `joeoakhart@navapbc.com` | claimed by the **outgoing** session via the parent-first cascade — see \"the epic's claim\" below |\n| `rollable-smoky-tsetsefly` | **closed** | the oversized-description blocker; resolved |\n| `deceitful-flannel-jerboa` | see its own trail | the review-kernel recall bug; resolved |\n| `bloated-shadeful-lamprey` | **`open`** — implemented, verified, **NOT landed** | released deliberately for the new session; full HANDOFF comment on that ticket |\n| the other **11** children | `open`, unstarted | nothing claimed, no worktrees, no commits |\n\n**Attestation:** this epic holds a signed plan-review PASS at `head_sha a147945aae`. It was\nalready re-signed once during this session for benign drift. Expect it to be **stale again** —\n`origin/main` has advanced at least to `d2dea317ec` since, and the epic's dependency set includes\n`docs/config.md`, which drifts often.\n\n## `bloated-shadeful-lamprey` — implemented but not landed\n\nThe only child with real work. Commit **`39c93ea3dc`** in worktree\n`/Users/joeoakhart/lamprey-libwrites` (branch `lamprey-libwrites`), clean, parent `d2dea317ec`.\nSplits `_lib_writes.py` 800 -> 378 / 280 / 231 by concern; proven **byte-identical** at the\ntop-level-block level; lint, typecheck, twelve `check_*` gates, the complexity `--lock` gate and\nall four generators green. Remaining: CI selection re-run from clean (it was **stopped mid-run at\n70% with zero failures** — treat as unrun), `tests/integration`, rebase, push, both +1s, submit,\nclose. Do not re-derive the split; read that ticket's HANDOFF comment first.\n\n## Dependency order for the 11 unstarted children\n\nSix are **roots** with no `depends_on` and can be worked in parallel — note that three of them\nare size-relief prerequisites, so they unblock the feature work:\n\n- `tasteful-historical-slug` — store-level project-to-repos mapping\n- `microbial-dicey-milksnake` — store-compat capability registration\n- `contrived-explicable-blobfish` — size relief: pagination cluster out of `fetcher`\n- `reunitable-preodorous-quelea` — size relief: `update_one` sub-tree\n- `bare-coed-thrasher` — size relief: STATUS cluster out of `reducer`\n- `bloated-shadeful-lamprey` — size relief: `_lib_writes` (**done, awaiting landing**)\n\nThen, in order:\n\n1. `buried-genial-gyrfalcon` (needs slug, lamprey, thrasher) — tri-state `bridge_project`/`repos`\n2. `algebraic-illstarred-mollusk` (gyrfalcon, blobfish) — multi-project inbound fetch\n   and `blitheful-deceitful-warbler` (slug, milksnake) — legacy-store migration\n3. `deathly-nondeadly-dorking` (gyrfalcon, quelea) — outbound dispatch + cross-project guard\n4. `unworldly-narrow-iggypops` (gyrfalcon, mollusk, dorking, warbler, milksnake) — docs + ADR 0062\n5. `gasolinic-microbian-puffin` — the live rehearsal; depends on **all 11**, so it is strictly last\n\nReview plans in this order too: a review pins its direct dependencies' material, so reviewing a\ndependent before its prerequisites wastes the LLM run.\n\n## Recovery recipe — benign code drift (works WITHIN one environment)\n\nWhen a claim fails with `the code the plan was reviewed against drifted: N dependency file(s)\nchanged (...)`:\n\n1. `rebar review-plan <id> --status` — read-only, **no LLM**. Confirms `verdict: stale-code` and\n   prints `verified_at_sha` and `currency_basis`.\n2. `rebar sign-review <id>` — re-signs from the recorded REVIEW_RESULT sidecar with **no LLM\n   re-run**, at current HEAD.\n\nThis is recovery, not a bypass: `sign-review` refuses when the **plan** changed, so it only ever\ncertifies across drift in files the plan did not depend on substantively. It was used twice this\nsession — once on lamprey (an attestation that PASSED but failed to persist, \"generation remained\nunstable after 3 attempts\") and once on this epic (drift from `a147945aae` touching\n`docs/config.md`). Try it before spending a full `review-plan`.\n\n## The epic's claim belongs to the OUTGOING session\n\nThis epic is left `in_progress` **deliberately** — the work is genuinely underway, and its child\n`lamprey` carries a real unlanded commit, so flipping the epic back to `open` would misrepresent\nthat. But the claim, the `claimed_session`, and the attestation's signing environment\n(`ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5`) all belong to a session that is ending.\n\nThe incoming session should **re-claim and re-cascade under its own environment**:\n\n- Its verification of both this epic's and lamprey's attestations will return **`foreign_key`**,\n  not `certified`. The claim gate fails closed on that, and **`sign-review` cannot fix it** — it\n  re-signs from a sidecar but does not cross environments.\n- So the new session must run a fresh `rebar review-plan 0e68-41eb-5782-4336` (and one for\n  whichever child it claims) with `REBAR_LLM_BEDROCK_REGION=us-east-1`. Both plans are settled and\n  passed cleanly, so expect clean PASSes with no plan edits — budget the LLM time, not a rewrite.\n- Do **not** reach for `claim --force` to paper over `foreign_key`. That bypasses the gate rather\n  than satisfying it, and AGENTS.md scopes `--force` to a human operator's judgment call.\n\nNothing here is closed, and no code was pushed anywhere."},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1786645445094582001,"uuid":"4ae49f10-ef74-42c3-8fe0-250b8d508033"}